  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Farmers, dairies and firms pay for reliable tests, healthier animals and safer products. They judge you by accuracy, ethics and practical results.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a clear, honest record of observations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and animal biotechnology: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools analyse genomic and imaging data. Routine analysis shrinks first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Welfare judgment, field understanding and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for data exploration; later, own the interpretation.
  </p>

